# Expandable Custom Plan rows and intermediary steps

Replace custom-row tap-to-view navigation with animated inline expansion and ordered construction-step statistics.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Tapping a custom plan main row expands it inline; tapping it again collapses it.
- [ ] Holding a custom plan row opens SCR-004-edit directly for that plan.
- [ ] Expansion and collapse animate subrows outward smoothly while lower plan rows move in synchrony.
- [ ] Each ordered construction action produces one intermediary subrow beneath its plan main row.
- [ ] Step subrows appear in exact plan order and use Road, Settlement, or City icons without redundant names.
- [ ] A clearly associated fixed-pane label identifies the group as `Steps`.
- [ ] Each step row uses the same Mean, Median, 25th, 75th, and turn-probability columns as main rows.
- [ ] Fixed labels/icons and scrolling values add/remove matching row heights so alignment is preserved throughout animation and scrolling.
- [ ] Cards-only plans with no construction steps omit the Steps section.
- [ ] Expansion state remains associated with stable plan identity across player filtering and All-player mode.
- [ ] Placeholder intermediary statistics are deterministic and red until simulation milestone output exists.
- [ ] Default-plan tap/hold behavior remains unchanged.
- [ ] Domain row-model and UI regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused animation/alignment checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- This supersedes TASK-013's custom-row tap-to-view behavior. Editing is now the long-press action specified by the updated SCR-002.
- Card-stat subrows are added separately by TASK-030 but share this task's expandable row model and synchronized panes.
